## Implementation Spec: Show Ideation Phase in Web UI

### File: server/templates/index.html

#### Task 1: Add ideation data attributes to feature cards in board_fragment template

**Location:** The `board_fragment` template define block (line ~799), inside the `<div class="feature-card">` element, after the existing `data-active` attribute (line ~813).

**Changes:** Add two new data attributes to each feature card div:

```
data-ideation="{{escapeAttr .Ideation}}"
data-ideation-summaries="{{toJSON .IdeationSummaries}}"
```

Insert these after the `data-done-script` attribute (line 812) and before `data-active`. This follows the same pattern used for other fields like `data-description` and `data-plan-reviews`.

**Dependencies:** None. The FeatureSummary struct already has `Ideation` (string) and `IdeationSummaries` ([]string) fields. The `escapeAttr` and `toJSON` template functions already exist.

#### Task 2: Update cardHash() to include ideation data

**Location:** The `cardHash()` function (line ~404) that generates a hash string for diffing card updates.

**Changes:** Add `c.getAttribute('data-ideation')` and `c.getAttribute('data-ideation-summaries')` to the array of attributes joined for the hash. This ensures the board auto-refresh detects changes to ideation content.

Change from:
```javascript
return [c.getAttribute('data-id'), c.getAttribute('data-stage'),
        c.getAttribute('data-title'), c.getAttribute('data-description'),
        c.getAttribute('data-history'), c.getAttribute('data-active')].join('|');
```

To:
```javascript
return [c.getAttribute('data-id'), c.getAttribute('data-stage'),
        c.getAttribute('data-title'), c.getAttribute('data-description'),
        c.getAttribute('data-history'), c.getAttribute('data-active'),
        c.getAttribute('data-ideation'), c.getAttribute('data-ideation-summaries')].join('|');
```

**Dependencies:** Task 1 (the attributes must exist on the cards).

#### Task 3: Add ideation rendering to showFeature() modal

**Location:** The `showFeature()` function, after the description section (line ~584) and before the history section (line ~585).

**Changes:** Add an ideation section that renders when ideation content is present. This follows the same pattern used in client.html (lines 851-857).

Insert this block after the description `if` block closes (after line 584):

```javascript
// Ideation section
var ideation = card.getAttribute('data-ideation') || '';
if (ideation) {
    html += '<div style="margin-top:0.75rem;padding-top:0.5rem;border-top:1px solid #21262d">' +
        '<div style="color:#8b949e;font-size:0.75rem;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:0.3rem">Ideation</div>' +
        '<div style="color:#c9d1d9;font-size:0.8rem;white-space:pre-wrap">' + escapeHtml(ideation) + '</div></div>';
}
// Ideation summaries (debate rounds)
try {
    var ideationSummaries = JSON.parse(card.getAttribute('data-ideation-summaries') || '[]');
    if (ideationSummaries && ideationSummaries.length > 0) {
        html += '<div style="margin-top:0.75rem;padding-top:0.5rem;border-top:1px solid #21262d">' +
            '<div style="color:#8b949e;font-size:0.75rem;font-weight:600;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:0.3rem">Ideation Summaries (' + ideationSummaries.length + ' rounds)</div>' +
            '<div style="max-height:300px;overflow-y:auto">';
        for (var si = 0; si < ideationSummaries.length; si++) {
            html += '<div style="font-size:0.75rem;padding:0.3rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #161b22">' +
                '<span style="color:#d2a8ff;font-weight:600">Round ' + (si + 1) + '</span>' +
                '<div style="color:#c9d1d9;white-space:pre-wrap;margin-top:0.2rem">' + escapeHtml(ideationSummaries[si]) + '</div></div>';
        }
        html += '</div></div>';
    }
} catch(e) {}
```

Key design decisions:
- The summaries container has `max-height:300px;overflow-y:auto` to handle potentially lengthy debate content without breaking the modal layout.
- Each round is numbered (Round 1, Round 2, etc.) so users can follow debate progression.
- Styling matches the existing dashboard modal patterns (same colors, font sizes, borders).
- Uses `escapeHtml()` for XSS safety (same as other sections).
- The ideation summaries are parsed from JSON (toJSON encodes []string) with a try/catch for robustness.

**Dependencies:** Task 1 (the data attributes must be present on the cards).

